  "factor": "other",
  "label": "not_comparable",
  "rationale": "Both extractions are faithful to their sources, and both concern body weight/BMI after the same exposure (Roux-en-Y gastric bypass) as within-group changes. However, the contrasts address non-overlapping phases of the postoperative weight trajectory: side A reports weight regain between 2 and 5 years after surgery (BMI rising to 31 kg/m2), while side B reports weight loss from baseline to month 12 (-24.1%, P < 0.001), with weight plateauing from month 12 to 24. The reference and outcome time points do not overlap, so the opposite directions (+ regain vs - loss) are not competing answers to the same question but descriptions of different post-surgical intervals. There is no common comparable contrast, so the pair is unfit for agreement/contradiction comparison; the decisive obstacle is the differing, non-overlapping time windows of the within-group weight changes."
